WEBVTT

00:05.660 --> 00:07.790
It's so hot!

00:22.230 --> 00:23.450
We've arrived.

00:26.100 --> 00:27.110
Akaike-san,

00:27.760 --> 00:29.110
I'm Hara from the Magic Office.

00:30.140 --> 00:31.080
Akaike-san?

02:21.650 --> 02:26.110
I see, so this young lady is a magic trainee then?

02:26.320 --> 02:29.350
Yes, but I'm still not very good...

02:29.030 --> 02:33.350
Speaking of being 16, that was the age when I first met that person.

02:33.830 --> 02:35.070
Is that so?

02:35.680 --> 02:38.670
Although I'm an old woman now, I still remember what it was like to be young.

02:40.640 --> 02:42.450
What kind of person was he?

02:43.540 --> 02:49.300
That's right, he always strictly wanted to keep his hair short and neat.

02:50.620 --> 02:53.230
He was a person with a smile like a flower.

02:56.110 --> 02:57.690
Love at first sight?

02:58.830 --> 03:02.690
Yes, that person said he was taken at first sight with me.

03:03.630 --> 03:05.040
That's a wonderful story.

03:05.730 --> 03:06.790
Um...

03:07.690 --> 03:12.250
in actuality, the trainee Suzuki will be performing the magic.

03:12.690 --> 03:13.960
We want to thank you very much.

03:14.170 --> 03:15.580
You're welcome.

03:15.920 --> 03:19.140
For today's magic action, I'll do my best and give it my all!

03:20.380 --> 03:22.950
I'm in your hands then.

03:25.690 --> 03:30.770
Although I've already made this request, I would like to have this returned back to its original form.

03:30.770 --> 03:32.560
What is this thing?

03:32.560 --> 03:34.340
A souvenir from that person.

03:39.770 --> 03:41.530
After World War II,

03:41.880 --> 03:46.900
a war buddy of his came to my place to give this to me.

03:47.970 --> 03:50.120
You mean these cinders?

03:50.530 --> 03:51.340
Yes,

03:51.700 --> 03:55.760
I thought why did he give me these though?

03:59.640 --> 04:03.160
That person died on an island in the south;

04:03.470 --> 04:06.130
he didn't surrender and died fighting to the end.

04:06.480 --> 04:09.630
The enemy's artillery was destroyed due to that.

04:09.880 --> 04:10.940
Oh my...

04:11.850 --> 04:13.850
That was war.

04:14.280 --> 04:16.820
Many people died because of it.

04:20.820 --> 04:21.740
But this is...

04:22.020 --> 04:25.950
this is a thing that that person couldn't stop talking about; that he held tightly in his hands.

04:27.890 --> 04:30.660
It had to be important since he kept holding it.

04:31.310 --> 04:34.210
Therefore, they thought if he returned back to Japan,

04:34.210 --> 04:37.440
he would deliver this to me at all cost.

04:38.500 --> 04:42.280
It really is an important thing, isn't it?

04:42.700 --> 04:45.380
Yes, I thought so too.

04:45.380 --> 04:47.190
So I thought it's something very important.

04:47.760 --> 04:52.780
But now you see, I'm at the time where I will pass away from the world soon.

04:53.360 --> 04:56.730
Although I could ask him directly then,

04:56.730 --> 05:01.980
but once I thought about it, I wanted to know exactly what it was.

05:04.650 --> 05:07.610
Although I said it's cinders...

05:07.610 --> 05:09.070
That's fine, that's fine.

05:09.670 --> 05:14.040
So then, I want you to return these cinders back to their original form.

05:15.430 --> 05:16.130
Okay!

05:18.770 --> 05:20.500
Akaike-san's magic request,

05:21.440 --> 05:24.310
is to return the souvenir back to its original form.

05:25.390 --> 05:26.720
The memory of the world,

05:27.620 --> 05:30.280
reveal the true form shrouded in the darkness of time,

05:30.770 --> 05:32.470
return back in time.

05:42.980 --> 05:43.690
Sensei!

05:44.010 --> 05:44.690
Don't stop!

05:45.270 --> 05:47.070
If you stop, it'll all vanish.

05:48.340 --> 05:49.470
I'll lend you my strength,

05:50.190 --> 05:51.320
don't stop the waves.

05:51.320 --> 05:51.950
Okay.

05:57.210 --> 05:57.860
Okay,

05:58.710 --> 05:59.720
you can stop the waves now.

05:59.940 --> 06:00.630
Okay.

06:07.250 --> 06:08.110
This is...

06:11.470 --> 06:14.540
this is what I gave him at the time he was sent off.

06:15.100 --> 06:17.680
He told me he wanted a souvenir from me.

06:19.250 --> 06:20.810
That person...

06:22.620 --> 06:26.030
during his last moments...

06:26.030 --> 06:28.250
was together with me, wasn't he...

06:29.380 --> 06:30.860
His last moments,

06:31.260 --> 06:34.310
he was thinking of me...

06:38.140 --> 06:39.020
I...

06:39.460 --> 06:43.300
I almost destroyed that important comb didn't I?

06:43.630 --> 06:44.320
Yeah...

06:45.150 --> 06:48.040
I failed as a mage.

06:50.970 --> 06:53.000
Sora-chan is a mage trainee, right?

06:53.350 --> 06:56.770
If you could do everything the first time, then you wouldn't need training.

06:56.770 --> 06:57.750
I see.

06:58.510 --> 07:01.130
Right now what you need is experience,

07:01.620 --> 07:03.520
magical powers differ by person.

07:04.490 --> 07:06.830
I think Sora-chan has really strong magical powers.

07:07.160 --> 07:10.710
Because when you brought back the comb, you were able to summon up a scene from the past.

07:12.820 --> 07:15.770
I really want to thank you for today.

07:16.100 --> 07:17.870
Because you were there, I...

07:17.870 --> 07:19.400
That is my job.

07:20.340 --> 07:23.020
Kikuko-obaachan was really happy.

07:23.390 --> 07:24.050
Yeah.

07:24.780 --> 07:27.430
It really was wonderful magic.

07:28.120 --> 07:29.460
There is the smile.

07:29.460 --> 07:30.220
Huh?

07:30.650 --> 07:32.330
Sora-chan's smile is the best.

07:33.300 --> 07:34.050
Okay!

07:34.050 --> 07:36.180
"Did you just laugh?"

07:39.400 --> 07:40.850
I'm so full.

07:40.850 --> 07:42.600
Thanks for the food.

07:42.780 --> 07:44.970
Thanks for the food, it was delicious.

07:46.700 --> 07:48.430
I'll go clean up.

07:48.910 --> 07:49.590
I will too.

07:50.570 --> 07:53.350
Then I'll leave it to the both of you.

07:53.360 --> 07:53.990
Okay!

07:54.800 --> 07:57.250
Gouta-kun doesn't like tomatoes?

07:58.140 --> 08:00.450
Ever since I was small, I've hated them.

08:00.450 --> 08:03.310
Hokkaido's tomatoes are really tasty.

08:03.770 --> 08:04.610
Hmm?

08:05.110 --> 08:07.920
At home, I would also make tomato juice.

08:08.780 --> 08:11.020
I want Gouta-kun to try it.

08:11.690 --> 08:12.970
Is it really that delicious?

08:12.970 --> 08:15.390
Yes, it's the best in the world!

08:16.690 --> 08:18.220
Then make it for me next time.

08:18.450 --> 08:19.810
Then come to Biei.

08:34.590 --> 08:35.990
Hokkaido, huh...

08:36.360 --> 08:38.080
must be a really beautiful place.

08:38.320 --> 08:40.830
You have to try Yoshiko-baachan's milk.

08:40.830 --> 08:43.900
Then you'll have to try an Enoshima shirasu-don.

08:44.390 --> 08:45.590
What is that?

08:45.910 --> 08:48.290
You don't know fresh sardines?

08:48.680 --> 08:50.460
Is that really delicious?

08:51.470 --> 08:52.590
Really delicious.

08:59.780 --> 09:01.760
The light of your sign is out.

09:01.760 --> 09:03.180
Ah, that huh?

09:03.180 --> 09:05.020
No need to be cheap with electricity.

09:05.020 --> 09:07.140
It's too troublesome.

09:19.480 --> 09:20.830
Delicious!

09:20.830 --> 09:21.910
Really?

09:21.910 --> 09:23.450
It really is!

09:23.450 --> 09:25.040
Ah, that makes me happy.

09:25.040 --> 09:27.170
That is goat's milk.

09:27.170 --> 09:27.970
For real?

09:28.280 --> 09:29.250
I'm lying.

09:31.390 --> 09:33.980
Yesterday, I drank too much so my head hurts.

09:43.710 --> 09:44.530
Good morning.

09:47.020 --> 09:48.230
Hey, Kuroda.

09:48.230 --> 09:48.940
Huh?

09:48.940 --> 09:49.520
What is it?

09:50.170 --> 09:53.190
About magic, how do you use it?

09:53.990 --> 09:55.460
A question all of a sudden?

09:55.810 --> 09:57.150
Well, it's fine.

09:57.650 --> 10:02.030
Let's see, for me I could already use it before I knew it.

10:02.030 --> 10:02.970
Liar.

10:03.320 --> 10:04.750
Asagi again?

10:05.160 --> 10:07.000
You can read people's minds?

10:07.630 --> 10:08.750
You know...

10:08.750 --> 10:14.090
suddenly being able to use magic, I have never heard of anyone able to do that.

10:14.090 --> 10:14.670
But...

10:14.670 --> 10:19.340
That's fine. Listen, magic is taught to you by your parents.

10:19.340 --> 10:22.980
By watching your parents, you remember how to use it.

10:23.570 --> 10:24.310
I see.

10:25.170 --> 10:27.060
Perhaps that works well too.

10:27.470 --> 10:30.540
Kuroda Koji, your parents taught you too, right?

10:30.790 --> 10:31.670
Parents, huh?

10:32.210 --> 10:34.880
Always acting so amazing, that Asagi...

10:35.340 --> 10:37.500
You're the liar, right?

10:37.750 --> 10:40.440
This time I'll let you call me the liar.

10:40.690 --> 10:42.900
Then please stop acting so cool.

10:43.280 --> 10:46.040
But I can understand what Honomi-chan is saying,

10:46.500 --> 10:50.690
because even birds learn by watching their parents fly.

10:51.320 --> 10:55.550
It's not the same comparing birds to humans.

10:55.550 --> 10:56.380
I see.

10:56.610 --> 10:58.310
So you learn from your parents...

11:04.330 --> 11:06.060
I can't do that...

11:06.770 --> 11:09.060
If it's not your parents, that's fine too.

11:09.060 --> 11:10.650
You can learn from expert mages.

11:13.830 --> 11:15.590
Expert mages...

11:22.920 --> 11:25.490
Ah, made it in time.

11:26.190 --> 11:27.120
Suzuki-san.

11:27.120 --> 11:27.890
Yes?

11:28.300 --> 11:31.960
Ah, I saw a cat family stuck in an alley,

11:31.960 --> 11:35.470
I took off my shoes and my handkerchief... and also...

11:34.250 --> 11:37.340
From tomorrow on, please be 5 minutes early to class.

11:37.690 --> 11:39.660
Yes, I'm sorry.

11:41.840 --> 11:42.790
What is it?

11:42.790 --> 11:44.060
You're so mean.

11:48.110 --> 11:51.050
I've already made up my mind, I can't go.

11:51.840 --> 11:53.310
A waking magic...

11:53.310 --> 11:54.630
in the evening, huh?

11:55.100 --> 11:56.070
What's the matter?

11:56.340 --> 11:57.440
Do you have something else to do?

11:57.440 --> 11:58.360
We'll both go.

11:59.010 --> 12:01.240
So it's quite difficult magic I see.

12:01.240 --> 12:03.700
I think it's a good opportunity to see Sora-chan's magical abilities.

12:03.700 --> 12:05.630
Yes, Sayori-chan has my vote.

12:05.640 --> 12:07.400
I told you to call me Sayori-obaasan!

12:10.160 --> 12:13.620
Ah Sei-san, what are you doing here so early?

12:13.620 --> 12:16.090
Today I'm girl surfing.

12:16.340 --> 12:17.700
What was that?

12:18.840 --> 12:21.620
Sei-san, what are you doing this afternoon?

12:21.840 --> 12:22.720
Getting a girl!

12:22.720 --> 12:23.920
No way.

12:24.650 --> 12:25.410
How's the store?

12:26.330 --> 12:27.600
Doing okay.

12:27.600 --> 12:28.780
Ah, not bad!

12:36.350 --> 12:38.100
Yo, Hayashi!

12:39.690 --> 12:40.360
Huh?

12:42.130 --> 12:43.720
No one's here.

13:11.070 --> 13:13.860
Sei-chan's guitar playing, been a while since I've heard that.

13:14.840 --> 13:18.190
It's this hot of a day and you're still wearing leather?

13:18.190 --> 13:20.980
I will wear leather even if the Earth becomes tropical.

13:23.090 --> 13:26.070
That Shunsuke has become a guitarist.

13:28.460 --> 13:31.060
You're his hero you know.

13:33.840 --> 13:35.570
Such a bothersome conversation.

13:37.800 --> 13:39.710
I saw his ads, it's tonight right?

13:40.250 --> 13:41.670
His first live.

13:41.670 --> 13:45.440
Hey, doesn't he look like the you from a long time ago?

13:45.840 --> 13:49.050
Tonight's live... I still have work to do.

13:49.050 --> 13:49.990
I see.

13:50.260 --> 13:51.860
If I finish work, I'll come on over.

13:52.170 --> 13:52.890
Okay.

13:54.040 --> 13:54.730
Hey.

13:56.150 --> 13:57.310
Get a wife.

13:57.310 --> 13:58.080
Huh?

13:58.290 --> 13:59.790
Having a family is a good thing.

14:00.000 --> 14:02.110
I'm getting by on my own.

14:02.110 --> 14:04.730
But you two can kiss anytime.

14:04.730 --> 14:07.170
Idiot, give my regards to Kayo-chan.

14:08.310 --> 14:09.150
Okay, then later.

14:13.210 --> 14:13.780
Then later.

14:13.780 --> 14:14.790
Do your best!

14:14.790 --> 14:15.500
Okay!

14:15.750 --> 14:17.370
We're seeing Motohashi-san.

14:17.370 --> 14:18.410
What?

14:18.410 --> 14:20.440
But it has nothing to do with vault magic.

14:21.620 --> 14:24.630
Um, can you give my regards to Motohashi-san?

14:24.630 --> 14:25.350
Okay.

14:30.810 --> 14:32.380
Waking magic...

14:33.570 --> 14:35.510
You're tense.

14:35.510 --> 14:36.260
Yes!

14:36.520 --> 14:37.310
Keep calm.

14:37.310 --> 14:37.940
Okay.

14:39.190 --> 14:41.280
Sora-chan's magic is strong.

14:41.710 --> 14:43.980
If you keep calm and composed, it'll be all right.

14:43.980 --> 14:44.700
Okay!

14:47.970 --> 14:51.360
My son has forgotten her voice.

14:51.780 --> 14:54.240
Even with watching the video from the sport's festival,

14:54.240 --> 14:56.200
he definitely has forgotten her voice.

14:57.490 --> 14:59.300
Ah sorry, sorry.

15:00.380 --> 15:03.360
Shion doesn't like me talking about him.

15:04.440 --> 15:08.530
I beg of you, please wake my wife.

15:13.240 --> 15:16.270
Shion-kun, I will wake your mom up, okay?

15:16.750 --> 15:17.600
Really?

15:17.600 --> 15:20.000
Yes, onee-chan will do her best.

15:21.570 --> 15:22.390
Okay.

15:22.390 --> 15:23.480
This person is?

15:23.480 --> 15:24.980
Suzuki Sora.

15:24.980 --> 15:28.520
She's a trainee but her magical powers are helpful.

15:28.810 --> 15:29.840
I'm sorry.

15:30.220 --> 15:31.540
It's because you looked so young.

15:32.550 --> 15:34.280
I'll give it my best.

15:35.040 --> 15:38.280
Then I leave my wife in your care.

15:43.010 --> 15:44.930
The doctors said she's comatose,

15:45.810 --> 15:47.670
an unconscious state.

15:48.260 --> 15:51.210
But it's been over a year and Miona has yet to wake.

15:53.080 --> 15:55.690
Then I'll perform magic on her consciousness.

15:56.430 --> 15:59.810
Then make sure it's the real consciousness.

16:01.720 --> 16:02.500
That's important.

16:04.500 --> 16:06.100
The wishes of the people waiting,

16:07.340 --> 16:09.360
accomplish in this person that is dear.

16:18.380 --> 16:19.060
Mama...

16:22.330 --> 16:23.210
Mama...

16:24.490 --> 16:25.180
Shion.

16:28.670 --> 16:29.420
Miona!

16:40.970 --> 16:41.740
Miona.

16:46.080 --> 16:46.920
That's great...

16:47.330 --> 16:48.900
You're aware now aren't you, Miona?

16:49.330 --> 16:50.120
Umm...

16:51.270 --> 16:52.440
I...

16:52.710 --> 16:54.320
Mama, it's me.

16:54.560 --> 16:56.970
I'm able to go to kindergarten by myself.

16:58.860 --> 16:59.730
Umm...

17:00.710 --> 17:02.370
Where is this place?

17:02.730 --> 17:03.490
Miona,

17:03.950 --> 17:05.830
Shion is now 5 years old.

17:07.320 --> 17:10.160
Who... are you?

17:14.760 --> 17:16.140
Sora-chan did well.

17:16.700 --> 17:17.390
But...

17:17.930 --> 17:20.080
why didn't her memories return?

17:20.510 --> 17:21.430
Well that's because...

17:22.030 --> 17:24.300
My magic isn't good enough then.

17:25.010 --> 17:26.450
That's where you're wrong.

17:26.710 --> 17:29.200
Kondo-san's request was revival magic.

17:29.440 --> 17:31.520
Beside, you completed what you had to do.

17:31.520 --> 17:32.340
But...

17:32.680 --> 17:36.870
Miona-san forgetting about Isao-san and Shion-kun, that shouldn't have happened!

17:37.240 --> 17:38.200
Sora-chan...

17:38.200 --> 17:39.630
It's not good at all!

17:40.770 --> 17:42.250
Without memories...

17:42.740 --> 17:47.480
all that were painful, all that were happy, they've all vanished.

17:48.370 --> 17:49.930
That is so sad...

17:50.540 --> 17:51.300
I...

17:51.870 --> 17:52.630
I...

17:52.630 --> 17:53.490
Sora-chan!

17:56.110 --> 17:58.260
I'm sorry, but...

17:58.260 --> 17:59.090
I...

18:01.130 --> 18:02.190
Magic...

18:02.690 --> 18:06.540
regardless of how skilled you are, it isn't a perfect thing.

18:07.070 --> 18:08.460
There are things that cannot be done.

18:08.990 --> 18:12.870
Sora-chan's magic granted the requestor's wish...

18:25.060 --> 18:27.290
Ah, Sei-chan has arrived.

18:27.690 --> 18:30.290
You're late, Seiichiro-san.

18:30.860 --> 18:33.540
I really wanted you to see our debut.

18:33.540 --> 18:36.340
I'm sorry, Aya-chan, a double please.

18:36.810 --> 18:39.260
My bass was the best.

18:39.260 --> 18:40.130
Idiot Haruna.

18:40.130 --> 18:42.070
The best is my guitar playing.

18:42.350 --> 18:45.680
Ah it has been a while since I've heard Shunsuke's guitar.

18:45.680 --> 18:47.690
Will you hear my drumming?

18:48.030 --> 18:49.650
Yes, yes, next time.

18:50.000 --> 18:51.020
You better!

18:51.340 --> 18:53.190
You had better come!

18:53.390 --> 18:54.570
Come!

18:56.730 --> 18:57.690
Good evening.

18:58.550 --> 19:00.030
Are you singing tonight?

19:00.260 --> 19:02.070
Yes, in a bit.

19:02.070 --> 19:03.510
I look forward to it.

19:03.830 --> 19:06.590
I really liked the jellyfish song.

19:07.330 --> 19:08.330
Thank you.

19:10.380 --> 19:12.780
How old are you?

19:13.090 --> 19:15.000
I'm 23.

19:15.710 --> 19:18.150
I see, 23.

19:18.840 --> 19:21.290
I realized it at tonight's live.

19:21.750 --> 19:23.140
Next years' Axe,

19:23.140 --> 19:28.220
in two years it'll be Fuji Rock and in 3 years it'll be Dome.

19:28.220 --> 19:30.600
Hey now, such a sparkling future isn't it?

19:31.340 --> 19:32.980
You look like someone from long ago.

19:32.980 --> 19:34.310
Who?

19:34.310 --> 19:37.210
You had done pretty well too.

19:37.530 --> 19:38.930
Ah, shut up.

19:39.520 --> 19:42.450
Huh, Seiichirou-san how far did you get?

19:42.950 --> 19:44.870
Just to Fuji.

19:44.870 --> 19:47.580
You definitely are amazing, Seiichirou-san.

19:56.320 --> 19:57.410
The future, huh?

20:07.060 --> 20:08.720
Bye bye.

20:09.800 --> 20:11.480
Seiichirou-san, see you later.

21:04.980 --> 21:07.920
Today's request was fun, wasn't it?

21:08.490 --> 21:12.960
I think I'll want to live a full life like Motohashi-san has.

21:13.450 --> 21:14.450
Yeah.

21:18.880 --> 21:21.490
That girl, did she go to sleep?

21:29.790 --> 21:30.900
Magic...

21:31.380 --> 21:33.020
is not perfect...

23:06.340 --> 23:09.350
On a sunny afternoon, during a break...

23:09.820 --> 23:12.680
On that day, I met a small girl.

23:13.560 --> 23:15.080
Next time, Friends.

23:15.770 --> 23:19.140
Mom, I made a new friend!
